What Scholarmind actually does:
ScholarMind (Semantic Search and Research Intelligence Engine) solves the problem of information overload in massive document repositories. Instead of a basic search bar that only matches exact keywords, it acts as an intelligent research assistant by understanding the context and intent behind a search. It actively "reads" relevant documents, generates a comprehensive cited summary, visually maps connections between topics, and learns from user interactions to proactively recommend documents.

Core Features:

-> Hybrid Search Engine
   - BM25 Sparse Retrieval: Handles exact-keyword matching.
   - Dense Vector Retrieval: Uses Transformer models to convert text into numbers and store them in pgvector.
   - Cross-Encoder Re-ranking: Re-scores top results for maximum accuracy.

-> Agentic RAG
   - LangGraph Orchestration: A multi-agent AI workflow that routes queries intelligently.
   - Corrective RAG (CRAG): Evaluates retrieved documents and rejects them if they don't contain the answer to avoid hallucination.

-> Knowledge Graph & Topic Modeling
   - Graph Relationships: Uses network algorithms to group related documents.
   - BERTopic Integration: Automatically identifies and extracts core themes.

-> Personalized Discovery
   - User Taste Vectors: Logs interactions to build a profile of interests.
   - Session-based Recommendations: Re-ranks results and populates a "For You" feed.

